  "text": "Recipe: Kathi Rolls\nCreator: Sharmila Vedam\nCategory: Kathi Roll\nIngredients: 3 medium sized sweet potatoes (boiled), Salt, Chilli powder, 1.5 tsp ajwain (carom seeds; crushed on my palm), 1 tsp coriander powder, 1 tsp Stuffed Paratha Powder, 100% King Arthur whole wheat flour, tofu cubes, homemade soy yogurt, turmeric powder, Tandoori Masala, homemade Green Chutney, Tamarind Date Chutney, purple cabbage, green cabbage, onion, cilantro, carrots\nCooking methods: boil, mash, pan-fry, air-fry\nInstructions: SWEET POTATO PARATHA: Mash cooked sweet potatoes with the rest of the ingredients. Then keep adding 100% King Arthur whole wheat flour till we get a soft roti dough consistency. Let it sit for 30 mins or so. Then make paratha on a non-stick griddle or cast iron tawa.\nBAKED TOFU: Marinate tofu cubes for 30 mins in a mixture of homemade soy yogurt, turmeric powder, chili powder, Tandoori Masala & salt to taste. Air fry for 7-8 minutes at 350 F. Then flip them over & air fry again for another 5 mins or so.\nKATHI ROLLS: Spread homemade Green Chutney and Tamarind Date Chutney on Sweet Potato Paratha. Add baked tofu, along with julienned raw veggies like purple & green cabbage, onion, cilantro, carrots.\nNotes: Sub-recipes: Sweet Potato Paratha, Baked Tofu, Green Chutney, Tamarind Date Chutney.\nA recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (whole wheat flour), BEANS (tofu, soy yogurt), TUBERS (sweet potato), RAINBOW VEGGIES (various), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
